## Why This Is Asked

Feature flags are ubiquitous in modern apps. This question probes practical testing across unit, integration, and end-to-end levels, plus resilience and data-driven CI—key for beginner-friendly interview depth.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and graceful fallback
- Mocking remote services for deterministic tests
- Data-driven CI with user segments
- Distinguishing unit, integration, and end-to-end coverage
- Handling retries and latency in test plans

## Code Example

```javascript
class FlagClient {
  constructor(fetchFn) {
    this.fetchFn = fetchFn;
    this.cache = null;
    this.ts = 0;
  }
  async isEnabled(flag) {
    const now = Date.now();
    if (this.cache !== null && now - this.ts < 60000) return this.cache;
    const val = await this.fetchFn(flag);
    this.cache = val;
    this.ts = now;
    return val;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend tests for multiple flags that might interact?
- How would you measure the cost of flag lookups in CI or production?

## Why This Is Asked
Explores testing considerations for feature flags and deployment safety, a practical beginner-level scenario relevant to modern cloud services.

## Key Concepts
- Flag-driven code paths and environment-based config
- Unit vs integration vs contract testing
- Canary/staging validation and rollback safety
- Deterministic data and payload coverage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Jest skeleton
describe('POST /process with flag', () => {
  test('uses A when USE_NEW_ALGO=false', async () => {
    process.env.USE_NEW_ALGO = 'false';
    const res = await request(app).post('/process').send({ input: 1 });
    expect(res.status).toBe(200);
    expect(res.body.algorithm).toBe('A');
  });
  test('uses B when USE_NEW_ALGO=true', async () => {
    process.env.USE_NEW_ALGO = 'true';
    const res = await request(app).post('/process').send({ input: 1 });
    expect(res.body.algorithm).toBe('B');
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt tests if the flag is sourced from a remote config service instead of env vars?
- What metrics would you collect to ensure the canary deployment remains within acceptable latency targets?
